  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Roadmap to Durable Solutions: Strengthening the Government of Colombia in the Implementation of the Durable Solutions Strategy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is based on the essential premise that providing durable solutions for the 8.5 million internally displaced persons in Colombia requires a strategic and coordinated approach among various actors. Over the next 18, this project will support and empower the Government in formulating a short- and medium-term strategy aimed at sustainably responding to Colombia&#x2019;s mass, protracted, and permanent internal displacement issues; thus, striving toward overcoming the Unconstitutional State of Affairs declared by the Constitutional Court since 2004. The strategy operates on two crucial fronts. First, it will assist the Government in defining and planning specific actions to address the complexities of displacement in Colombia with a territorial approach. This strategic planning process will provide the Government with a solid framework informed by consistent technical data and a road map to handle durable solutions realistically and adaptively to IDP&#xb4;S. Second, active support will be provided to identify and coordinate actions towards lasting solutions in 3 targeted territories.</narrative>
  </description>
